%% Source for how-it-works.png on /docs/apis/workload-identity-federation.
%% Regenerate the PNG from the repository root with the Inter font installed. The second command adds the bottom margin that Mermaid leaves out:
%%   npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli@11 -i images/docs/apis/workload_identity_federation/how-it-works.mmd -o images/docs/apis/workload_identity_federation/how-it-works.png -b white -s 2
%%   magick images/docs/apis/workload_identity_federation/how-it-works.png -background white -gravity south -splice 0x36 -strip images/docs/apis/workload_identity_federation/how-it-works.png
%% The PNG's width and height must both be even numbers. Update the width and height in pages/apis/workload_identity_federation.md to half of them.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant W as Workload
    participant P as OIDC provider
    participant T as Buildkite token<br/>exchange endpoint
    participant A as Buildkite<br/>REST API
    W->>P: Request an OIDC token
    P-->>W: Signed OIDC token
    W->>T: Client ID and OIDC token
    Note over T: Check the token against<br/>the workload identity
    T-->>W: bkwi_ access token
    W->>A: API request with the bkwi_ token
    Note over A: Check the token's<br/>pipeline access and scopes
    A-->>W: API response for allowed pipelines
